## Status

Accepted

## Context

If you make a log like this:

```js
class ConsoleLog {
    constructor(opts = {}) {
        this._opts = { allowTrace: false, ...opts };
    };

    info(message) {
        console.log(message);
    }

    trace(message) {
        console.log(`ths: ${this}`);
        if (this._opts.allowTrace) {
            console.log(message);
        }
    }
}
```

and then pass a reference to `trace` to another function, `trace` fails because `this` is undefined.

